-- classify counts the passing cases each class holds (classes can overlap); cover asks a class for a share of them
under test: number
let numerals = [0 .. 9]
law classes_proved: all n: number(n). n >= 0 by exhaustion classify zero when n = 0, small when n < 5
law classes_tested: all n: number(n). n >= 0 by test classify always when n >= 0
law classes_let: all n: number(n), let m = n * 2. m >= n by exhaustion classify big when m > 10
law covered: all n: number(n). n >= 0 by exhaustion classify zero when n = 0 cover 10% zero
law undercovered: all n: number(n). n >= 0 by exhaustion classify zero when n = 0, small when n < 5 cover 20% zero, 50% small, 60% small
law refuted_classes: all n: number(n). n < 5 by exhaustion classify zero when n = 0
law cover_unknown: all n: number(n). n >= 0 by exhaustion classify zero when n = 0 cover 5% big
law cover_over: all n: number(n). n >= 0 by exhaustion classify zero when n = 0 cover 120% zero
